Z||000006||NOS3800||08-13-2001||06:39 PM||||Well, my car is driven everyday and it has NOS, along with a Series II 3800 and 4 speed auto. With the 75 shot I am running 13.5's. However i recently reworked the nozzle(placement) and it runs even better now! Unfortunately the weather hasn't permitted me to get any new numbers. It should be well into the low 13's. My 60ft times are 1.9's but will DEFINITELY be better now cause the NOS now engages right off the line, where before it didn't engage till 20ft or so. I will get my brother to post his numbers. He has a 3800SC motor.<BR>What are your trap speeds and what was teh weather like? I thought you would be into the low 13's also, since you have 300 HP.<P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.58@99.08 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||1
Z||000007||Jay||08-13-2001||06:45 PM||||It was quit hot out about 80 degrees with no tail wind.  The performance shift select will help out alot also.  I can't wait to go on a nice cool evening.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Slammed Fiero||08-13-2001||06:46 PM||||I don't think that his mid 13's are the best. I remember riding in Chris moores car , which turned nearly identical times at the strip. The car seemed like a slug (sorry chris) off the line , then it hit about 25-30mph and slammed you back in the seat. The powerband is so progressive on those motors with No flat spots, reminded me a lot of a 911 , power everywhere above 2500rpm.<P>I think tuning is a huge issue with N*'s. and specifically the computer. Keep in mind it's setup for a Cushy caddy driver , not meant to shift hard and snap necks.<P>Hope someone figures it out.<P>Right now I need some rear tires, My 255/40's are corded. I'm going hunting this weekend for a set of used Autocross compound tires.<P>1FST2m6 got his 4spd 2.8 with NOS into the 13's. Shaun 41178 did it with an auto and street tires (14.1) so we will see if perhaps I can put on a good NOS show.<P>I don't see how some people with built 3.1+ ltr engines and NOS are only running 15's... you know who I mean....<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, White face Gauges , 70Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
