Z||000014||lildevil||08-13-2001||07:37 PM||||Great to hear about your times Jay. Tell me were you spinning tires any off the line?  My 3.8 SC 85 Fiero  ran a best of 13.311 @ 100.75 mph last month.  I have since ran that number 3 times at Maple Grove 3 weeks ago.  And my car is spinning off the line but it still gets 1.8 60 foot times.  When it get cooler say 50 degrees. Look out. Our cars could be in the twelves.  In comparison to your Northstar, the 3.8  has more torque off the line...hence the faster 60 foot times. Where the Northstar has an advantage is up high in t he RPM range due to the extra cylinders and overhead cams.  Thats why your mph is higher.  I would love to race a Northstar Fiero side by side with  my car  one day jus to see how they compare.<P>------------------<BR>Earl Sessions<BR>1985 Fiero w/ 1998 Supercharged 3.8 V-6<BR>Best ET: 13.311 @100.75 mph<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000015||Jay||08-13-2001||08:47 PM||||I don't spin much off the line, lots of grip.  The problem is that I got no e-brake and it's hard to heat up the tires without one.  I'm also running a pretty hard street tire (Khumo Ecsta Supra's...17").  I beat anything off the line, lots of torque...no problems there.  I think I need more top end, cause that's where everyone takes me...at the line. ||||reg||1
Z||000016||jelly2m8||08-13-2001||10:38 PM||||A local with an Archie conversion, 350 sbc & 3.32 4 spd ran a 13.186 @ 104.2 mph at  the track yesterday.<P> Wayne wasn't able to get it lower, only because he eliminated himself on his first run. I'm not sure how this bracket racing works, but I believe he though he would only be able to run a 13.30 at best, and apparently you can't run any faster than your dial in time is. If thats what you call it. <P> Still, I though this was pretty acceptable, as the modded Mudstains and Camaros were running in the mid to low 14's. <P> Were pretty sure that with some more practice, and maybe lowering the tire pressure that the car will run in the 12's. Maybe next time we will see.<P> Hopefully next time I will get a change to take my V8 to the track and give that a run.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Jay||08-13-2001||11:23 PM||||Yes in bracket racing you win if you are closer to your dial in time without going faster.  example if you dial in at 13.5 and then run a 13.49 you are eliminated.  It doesn't really matter how fast, it's more how well you know your car.  In bracket racing if you are dialed in at 13.5 and your opponent is dialed in at 15.5 he gets a 2 second head start, so that technically you should both finish at about the same time.  However, if you (13.5) cross the line before the other guy (15.5) who has the head start, and don't "break out" then you win regardless of wheather or not 15.5 is closer to his dial in.  Basically you are racing against yourself, not really against the guy beside you.  I think I may have made that more complicated than it is. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000018||Smoooooth GT||08-13-2001||11:29 PM||||GREAT TIMES...  I just bought that NOS kit from Shaun41178...  I can't wait to get to the track...  well, I guess I have to finish the bodywork first...  <BR>I have a question...   Will the SC from the series 2 3800's fit on a series one 3800???<P>------------------<BR>NEW EMAIL..  Smooth_gt@k.st<BR>ADD on's Now...  Shaun's NOS Kit.. :)<BR>Future add's.. 2" drop, 17" wheel's, finish the turbo T-3watercooled project, ViperYellow          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig2_3.JPG"> ||||reg||1
