Z||000020||NOS3800||08-13-2001||11:35 PM||||Jay,<BR>Are you power braking at the light? That will dramatically improve your 60' ft times. My 3800 (205 HP) has 2.1 sec 60 ft times, so your 2.0 60's aren't too impressive, it should be lower. But I guess we need to take into account weight. Takes alot to get things rolling, those 4T80 trannies are heavy!<BR>Also, you said you don't have an e-brake. Why do you need that to do a burnout? With the auto, mash the brakes, push the gas then slowly release the brake till you get wheel spin, then hold the brake there and then push gas harder. Use two feet (of course) and works best right outside of the water box.||||reg||1
Z||000021||Jay||08-13-2001||11:41 PM||||NOS3800 I need to really ugrade my front brakes.  I've got S/S lines and cross drilled rotors (stock fiero) but it's not  enough to hold the car, it's all over the place.  Maybe I just need more practice! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I also haven't changed the tach over to read 8 cylinders so I can only go by ear.  I figure I'm reving around 2500 or so when I launch but I can't be sure.  That's next on the list of to do's.||||reg||1
Z||000022||NOS3800||08-14-2001||12:19 AM||||As far as I know, and I am on the Grand Prix list, The Series II blower only works on the Series II supercharged motor. It WILL NOT bolt up too the NA 3800 motor, they flame everyone who asks, and it gets asked alot. I there fore do not think it will bolt to the Series one block either. From my searching no one has ever done it. The heads are different for each motor, and to modify the motors so they will accept the blower would cost WAY more then just getting a used SC 3800 Series II.||||reg||1
Z||000023||Smoooooth GT||08-14-2001||12:39 AM||||Thank's everybody for the answer...  My brother has a Bonneville w/ a series 1 and wanted to know...  thank's again...   <BR>I  have another ?.....  <BR>I just bought that NOS kit from Shaun as I said before...  Can I modify the kit, or the jet's to get into 13's???  I don't know if he was pushing it or not...   anyone know???  Thank's Steve||||reg||1
Z||000024||Cheever2||08-14-2001||12:40 AM||||hugh, what's that big ol' engine you got under your scoop?  Have you taken it to the strip?  What does it do?<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000025||NOS3800||08-14-2001||12:53 AM||||Smoooooth, Need some details... If Shaun ran a 14.1 with auto, if you are running a manual tranny you will be well within the 13's. What is your car running motor wise? What kind of shot will you be using(50HP,60HP,75HP etc...)? If you are running the same motor and trans as Shaun, run the exact same shot he used. Go to the track and see what you run, you may run faster simply because your "track" is faster. If you don't, then change the pills to a higher HP. Be careful though, I wouldn't go any higher the 100HP on a high mileage motor!<BR>GOOD LUCK! Let me know how you do! You can email me with any questions too. ||||reg||12
Z||000026||Shaun41178||08-14-2001||01:42 AM||||Smoooth, I mailed the extra nitrous jets with the kit.  They are in the envelope with your address on it so don't throw it away or you will be throwing away extra jets.  The jets in the kit right now is setup to give you a 70 shot.<P>the .032 jet is a 50 shot, a .036 is a 70 shot, a .040 is a 90 shot.  <P>I used the 70 shot at the track all the time.  I got a best of a 14.2 at 90 mph with the 70 shot.  I would powerbrake my tranny as high as it would go(roughly 1800 rpm) without the car moving forward.  I would arm the nitrous system, last amber flashes and I slam the gas and let off the brake at the same time.  I would get consistent 1.8-1.9 60' times on tiny 205/60/14 tires.  <P>I used the 90 shot pill once and was able to get a 14.1 at 89 mph.  I am sure that if I had a shift kit or a 2.5 inch exhaust I would have run a 13.9. <P>My other mods included underdrive pulley, crane ignition box with coil and accel 8.8 mm wires and stock heat range delco plugs gapped to .050.  Without a high output ignition I would go with .035 gap.  I also had a brass prong distributor cap instead of the aluminum as brass is a better conductor.  Bypassed TB, bypassed PCV, CAI, ported exhaust manifolds, and a rear sway bar to help with the launching.  Before I added the bar I noticed very slight wheel hop but after the bar I just dead hooked.  My fuel system was totally stock.<P>Smooth I would go higher then a 90 shot on your engine.  in fact I wouldn't recommend higher then a 70 actually unless you have tons of fuel and enough ignition retard.  I can say that with a 90 I was pushing my car.  I was scared I was going to blow it when I ran the 90 and I had a pretty fresh motor.<P>And I can say that I raced at a fast track.  Norwalk is a pretty fast track at least I think it is.<P>Little tricks I would do is take out the pass seat and spare tire and jack, raise tire pressure in the front tires to 45 psi, rears dropped to 27 psi, and iced the intake before each run.  Since I have an auto I disconnected my TCC lockup switch and I got about .1-.2 faster after doing that<P>Smooth if you have any questions I sent you some info on the back of one of my dyno sheets with my phone number and all that in case you want to talk to me.  AIM is Shaun41178<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds||||reg||1
Z||000027||Smoooooth GT||08-14-2001||04:11 PM||||Shaun..... I GOT IT..........YESSSSSSSSS...lol   <BR>Thank's for all the advise everybody, I'LL USE IT TOO. <BR>I'm running a stock internal(sp?) But, I have MSD 6A ignition, MSD Blaster coil, 8.8mm wires, intake simular to Shaun's with the cone(K&N), stock fuel system, bored and polished Throttle Body, I matched the intake gasket's, bored and cleaned out ex. manifold's. There's a little more but, I can't think right now(NOS on the brain)LOL<BR>Shaun you did'nt sent a .36 jet, you sent a .32, .38,.40...   What shot is the .38 jet??  <P>NOS3800...  I have a auto trans. also...  I'm not sure which jet I'll run, probably the one Shaun already has in there(70 shot)..  <BR>I'll let everybody know when I get to rujn it...    Thank's again Shaun..   I love you man...lol   Steve<P>------------------<BR>NEW EMAIL..  Smooth_gt@k.st<BR>ADD on's Now...  Shaun's NOS Kit.. :)<BR>Future add's.. 2" drop, 17" wheel's, finish the turbo T-3watercooled project, ViperYellow          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig2_3.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000028||Shaun41178||08-14-2001||05:31 PM||||Glad it made it there in one piece Steve.  God Bless the US postal service.<P>The .036 jet is already in the nozzle that goes into the intake opening.  There is a little blue nozzle on the end of the smaller nitrous braided line coming off the solenoids.  If I am not mistake unscrew the little blue nozzle and the .036 jet should be inside it.  if it is not then I apologize and must have lost it.  The .038 jet is a 80 shot.  <P>You have a few more mods then I do Steve so you just might be able to run in the high 13's.  You better 3.33 FD should help some too.  I would recommend gutting your cat or removing it if the law doesnt' check that stuff and or go to a 2.5 catback system.  With that and a shift kit I have no doubt that you can run 13's with my x-kit.  Keep an eye on the air/fuel ratio.  I wuld recommend a gauge.<P>Steve I just noticed that I forgot to mail the bottle mounting brackets to you.  I am such a dork!!  Doh!!  I will get them out to you as soon as possible.<P>Call or email if you have any quesitons about what goes where or the wiring at all of it.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds||||reg||1
